{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/116911-lunar-virtue-flaws-give-me-yours","id":116911,"title":"Lunar Virtue Flaws - give me yours!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-21T06:37:37-07:00","id":116911,"title":"Lunar Virtue Flaws - give me yours!","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I have managed to find with a Google search plenty of custom Solar Virtue Flaws, but it seems hard to find custom Lunar ones. I have in fact only seen one on <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/\" target=\"_blank\">http://exalted.xi.co.nz/</a>, and five more from &quot;The Journal of Bone and Ebony&quot;. Does anyone have any other custom Lunar Virtue flaws?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T06:53:22-07:00","id":116918,"title":"","content":"They do seem to be a rarity, though it's also not so much a problem. They're essentially &quot;Solar Limit Breaks with an animal thematic,&quot; so one can certainly just do some refluffing of any Solar Virtue Flaws floating around.<br /> <br /> That said, I did make this one for an incredibly short-lived Lunars game I was in... wow, almost 4 years ago. o_o <span style=\"font-size:9px\">That's just stupid...</span><br /> <br /> Anyway, kind of uninspired, but here ya go:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><u>Curse of the Father Wolf</u></b> (Compassion)<br /> The character is overcome with raw protective instinct. Real or perceived threats to his 'pups' (living Intimacies, children, and others he is inclined to protect) are met without restraint. The Father Wolf is heedless of other potential consequences. The character will cast off a disguise if it inhibits this protection, see that any aggressors never live to be dangers again, and will give his own life in defense, if he must.<br /> <b>Partial Control:</b> The character is plainly aggressive to threats, but understands an unrestrained jump into harm's path may not be the best means of protection. The Father Wolf will take action, but this need not be immediate, and may be done without sacrificing subtlety, by disabling a foe without deadly force or by offering conciliatory negotiation, or simply by fleeing with the pups.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: Dusk Shine reminded me that I'd forgotten the actual Virtue; this one was Compassion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Added Virtue. 04-21-2014, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T07:02:57-07:00","id":116923,"title":"","content":"I once wrote up &quot;Curse of the Aloof Cat&quot;, which made Lunars unable to act on anything unless it posed an immediate threat to themselves. Partial control allowed them to also act on immediate threats to motivation and intimacies. Either way, they ignored all long-term consequences, and always took the &quot;quick and easy&quot; solution. <br /> Now if I only remembered which virtue I keyed it to...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T09:07:54-07:00","id":116980,"title":"","content":"Curse of the Beta Male<br /> Valor-based, the Lunar could not stand being a subordinate to anyone (though s/he could tolerate being subordinate to ideals beyond self-interest), and sought an appropriately difficult challenge based on his Intimacies to prove his/her dominance over others in his/her group.<br /> Ex. &quot;You're the Gray Fox. You're wanted for.... for... all kinds of things. I'LL MAKE CAPTAIN FOR THIS!&quot; -Elder Scrolls: Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:01:39-07:00","id":117042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/116911-lunar-virtue-flaws-give-me-yours#post116911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and five more from &quot;The Journal of Bone and Ebony&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are <a href=\"http://boneandebony.livejournal.com/tag/lunar%20virtue%20flaw\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, for those of you who do not know the Journal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}